From f1ba041c61005f68447849e232301bb1a6803a6e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TeamHarrisCali <34009957+TeamHarrisCali@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 11:01:23 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] DSi Wi-Fi chip: firmware upload (BMI) from the DSi's own
 firmware file

w98h: the chip answers (AR6013, boot ROM 0x23000024, 4-bit bus) but has no
firmware after Unlaunch. Upload it:
- ARM7 (twlwifi.c): a run without firmware stays in BMI with the antenna on
  the Atheros chip ("held"); request ops 2-9: write memory, LZ stream start,
  LZ data, execute, set app start, write a word, finish (start + wait),
  release.
- ARM9 (new dsiwifi.c, /proc/dsiwifi2 moved from volume.c): /proc/dsiwifi2fw
  takes the firmware file (title HNCA, WLFIRM); "echo upload > /proc/dsiwifi2"
  runs, picks the blob for the chip ID and boot ROM version, writes parts 2
  and 5, executes 5, LZ-streams part 1, sets the app start, writes part 4
  and points hi_dset_list_head at it, starts the firmware, waits for
  hi_board_data_initialized, releases the antenna; an upload log is shown.
- wifi-dsi-test feeds /usr/lib/firmware/dsi-wifi.bin when present.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
